WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:35.041


2
00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:36.458
<b>In the Bhagavad Gita,</b>

3
00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:40.541
<b>only Sri Krishna is referred to as</b>
<b>Bhagavan (God).</b>

4
00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:47.708
<b>It is His divine teachings that have been</b>
<b>guiding humanity for thousands of years.</b>

5
00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:52.666
<b>In response to Arjuna's dilemma,</b>
<b>his numerous doubts, and his questions,</b>

6
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:56.666
<b>Lord Sri Krishna now begins to speak here.</b>

7
00:00:56.666 --> 00:00:58.083
<b>He says:</b>

8
00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:59.291
<b>"O Arjuna!</b>

9
00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:06.375
<b>At this decisive moment, what kind of</b>
<b>weakness and impurity has arisen in your mind?</b>

10
00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:10.250
<b>This is entirely inappropriate for an Aryan.</b>

11
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:15.416
<b>This will lead not to heaven, but to disgrace."</b>

12
00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:20.250


13
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:26.166
<b>Lord Sri Krishna is expressing surprise</b>
<b>at Arjuna's arguments and thoughts here.</b>

14
00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:28.250
<b>At such a crucial time,</b>

15
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:32.041
<b>for a great wise and virtuous warrior like Arjuna</b>

16
00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:36.375
<b>it was not at all expected</b>
<b>to become so distressed.</b>

17
00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:40.625
<b>That's why Krishna calls it impurity here.</b>

18
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:43.291
<b>Clean water is transparent,</b>

19
00:01:43.291 --> 00:01:43.958
<b>but</b>

20
00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:47.583
<b>if dust or soil mixes in, or if some color is added,</b>

21
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:51.416
<b>then it becomes difficult</b>
<b>to see through that water.</b>

22
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:52.750
<b>Similarly,</b>

23
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:58.958
<b>when our perspective becomes polluted,</b>
<b>everything starts to look wrong.</b>

24
00:01:58.958 --> 00:02:00.875
<b>Arjuna is a warrior,</b>

25
00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:03.791
<b>and when this great war is all set,</b>

26
00:02:03.791 --> 00:02:10.625
<b>it is necessary that he supports</b>
<b>dharma and fulfills his duty as a warrior.</b>

27
00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:11.750
<b>But</b>

28
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.000
<b>in this situation, he is abandoning his weapons.</b>

29
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.208
<b>Such thinking,</b>

30
00:02:16.208 --> 00:02:18.416
<b>such behavior is uncultured,</b>

31
00:02:18.416 --> 00:02:19.708
<b>un-Aryan.</b>

32
00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>It doesn't befit</b>

33
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.250
<b> an Aryan like Arjuna.</b>

34
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:24.666
<b>Here, </b>

35
00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:28.625
<b>the word 'Aryan' doesn't refer</b>
<b>to any particular class,</b>

36
00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:32.333
<b>nor to people from any geographical area.</b>

37
00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:36.291
<b>'Aryan' here refers to the word 'Arya'.</b>

38
00:02:36.291 --> 00:02:39.708
<b>Arya means spiritually evolved,</b>

39
00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:40.500
<b>ideal, </b>

40
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.291
<b>righteous, </b>

41
00:02:41.291 --> 00:02:42.416
<b>virtuous.</b>

42
00:02:42.416 --> 00:02:46.458
<b>A person who is Arya in conduct is an 'Aryan'.</b>

43
00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:49.250
<b>Krishna is referred to as Bhagavan here.</b>

44
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:55.416
<b>The word Bhagavan is formed by</b>
<b>combining the Sanskrit words "Bhaga" and "van".</b>

45
00:02:55.416 --> 00:02:57.750
<b>Bhaga means prosperity, </b>

46
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.208
<b>van means 'ownership of something'.</b>

47
00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:04.833
<b>So Bhagavan is one who</b>
<b>is the master of prosperity.</b>

48
00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:09.500
<b>Vyasadeva's father, sage Parashar,</b>
<b>mentioned six prosperities.</b>

49
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.125
<b>These prosperities are</b>

50
00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:11.958
<b>wealth,</b>

51
00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.958
<b>beauty,</b>

52
00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:13.916
<b>fame,</b>

53
00:03:13.916 --> 00:03:14.875
<b>knowledge, </b>

54
00:03:14.875 --> 00:03:15.750
<b> power,  </b>

55
00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.416
<b>and renunciation. </b>

56
00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:21.875
<b>While some or the other prosperity,</b>
<b>in small or large measure,</b>

57
00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:24.416
<b>is possessed by every distinguished person,</b>

58
00:03:24.416 --> 00:03:31.708
<b>Bhagavan (God) is only the one who has</b>
<b>complete mastery over all these prosperities. </b>

59
00:03:31.708 --> 00:03:33.500
<b>Like Bhagavan (God),</b>

60
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.458
<b>Sri Krishna.</b>

61
00:03:36.041 --> 00:03:40.291


62
00:03:40.291 --> 00:03:43.958
<b>Just as life is impossible without water,</b>

63
00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:47.333
<b>and a river provides water,</b>

64
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:50.500
<b>giving life, </b>

65
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.458
<b>but</b>

66
00:03:52.458 --> 00:03:54.000
<b>that same river,</b>

67
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.375
<b>if it goes out of control,</b>

68
00:03:57.375 --> 00:03:59.875
<b>can take the form of a flood,</b>

69
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:04.000
<b>washing everything away.</b>

70
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.041
<b>Similarly,</b>

71
00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:11.041
<b>ife is not possible without emotions.</b>

72
00:04:11.041 --> 00:04:16.500
<b>They are an integral part of life.</b>

73
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.500
<b>However,</b>

74
00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.541
<b>if those same emotions</b>

75
00:04:19.541 --> 00:04:24.083
<b>become uncontrolled and start surging,</b>

76
00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:29.375
<b>their flood will make life miserable.</b>

77
00:04:29.375 --> 00:04:35.791
<b>The emotions that Arjuna was calling</b>
<b>compassion, righteousness, and familial love,</b>

78
00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:38.833
<b>considering withdrawing from the battle,</b>

79
00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:44.166
<b>I could see flaws and</b>
<b>impurities in those very emotions.</b>

80
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:45.458
<b>Because</b>

81
00:04:45.458 --> 00:04:46.625
<b>somewhere</b>

82
00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:49.166
<b>behind all these emotions,</b>

83
00:04:49.166 --> 00:04:58.083
<b>Arjuna had completely forgotten his responsibility</b>
<b>towards social welfare and dharma.</b>

84
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:01.875
<b>He wanted to back out of the battle,</b>

85
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:02.875
<b>but</b>

86
00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:08.041
<b>he could not think that just by his withdrawal,</b>

87
00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:11.125
<b>the battle would not be averted.</b>

88
00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:12.083
<b>Rather,</b>

89
00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:17.583
<b>by doing so, those unrighteous Kauravas</b>
<b>would become even more powerful.</b>

90
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.708
<b>So, if the</b>

91
00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:21.916
<b>battle will not be averted,</b>
<b>if adharma will not be averted,</b>

92
00:05:21.916 --> 00:05:27.500
<b>then who will benefit from Arjuna's withdrawal?</b>

93
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:33.708
<b>This is a very narrow perspective, isn't it?</b>

94
00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:36.083
<b>For this reason, it was necessary</b>

95
00:05:36.083 --> 00:05:41.666
<b>for me to tell Arjuna in clear</b>
<b>words that such impurity</b>

96
00:05:41.666 --> 00:05:44.791
<b>does not befit him.</b>

97
00:05:44.791 --> 00:05:50.625
<b>Arjuna was clothing his hidden emotions</b>
<b>in the garb of reasoning. </b>

98
00:05:50.625 --> 00:05:52.625
<b>And this happens every time,</b>

99
00:05:52.625 --> 00:05:54.375
<b>many times, </b>

100
00:05:54.375 --> 00:06:00.416
<b>that when we are about to do</b>
<b>something wrong, or are anxious, </b>

101
00:06:00.416 --> 00:06:07.583
<b>we start justifying every decision</b>
<b>of ours by giving reasons.</b>

102
00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:10.166
<b>The more difficult the situation,</b>

103
00:06:10.166 --> 00:06:16.458
<b>the more important emotional balance</b>
<b>becomes for a person.</b>

104
00:06:16.458 --> 00:06:24.583
<b>It is necessary to make decisions from</b>
<b>the perspective of wisdom, dharma, and duty.</b>

105
00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:32.041
<b>It is essential to keep the river of</b>
<b>emotions controlled between its two banks.</b>

106
00:06:32.583 --> 00:06:36.750


107
00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:38.333
<b>The weakness of the mind</b>

108
00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:40.041
<b>and uncontrolled emotions</b>

109
00:06:40.041 --> 00:06:42.250
<b>not only hinder us </b>

110
00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.083
<b>but also</b>

111
00:06:43.083 --> 00:06:48.708
<b>affect our family and the people around us. </b>

112
00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:51.291
<b>Just think,</b>

113
00:06:51.291 --> 00:06:56.291
<b>the entire army of the</b>
<b>Pandavas, ready to fight, is standing, </b>

114
00:06:56.291 --> 00:06:57.083
<b>and in such a situation,</b>

115
00:06:57.083 --> 00:07:02.541
<b>how devastating can the effect of</b>
<b>their greatest warrior Arjuna's</b>

116
00:07:02.541 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>weak thought of abandoning</b>
<b>the war be on their morale.</b>

117
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:08.666
<b>Similarly,</b>

118
00:07:08.666 --> 00:07:11.625
<b>we live in society and family,</b>

119
00:07:11.625 --> 00:07:18.166
<b>and in such a situation, we cannot shirk</b>
<b>our responsibilities towards others. </b>

120
00:07:18.166 --> 00:07:22.125
<b>It is necessary that emotions are in your control,</b>

121
00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:27.666
<b>rather than you being in the grip of emotions.</b>

122
00:07:27.666 --> 00:07:29.375
<b>To do this,</b>

123
00:07:29.375 --> 00:07:30.833
<b>meditation is necessary,</b>

124
00:07:30.833 --> 00:07:33.041
<b>spirituality is necessary,</b>

125
00:07:33.041 --> 00:07:37.583
<b>to strengthen the mind and</b>
<b>decision-making power,</b>

126
00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:42.958
<b>reading the teachings and</b>
<b>articles written is necessary.</b>

127
00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:44.875
<b>This is not just a personal duty,</b>

128
00:07:44.875 --> 00:07:47.583
<b>but a social one as well.</b>

129
00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:52.333


130
00:07:52.333 --> 00:07:53.791
<b>Leader.</b>

131
00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:56.958
<b>The word "leader" is derived</b>
<b>from the term "leadership." </b>

132
00:07:56.958 --> 00:08:00.458
<b>Whether in a</b>

133
00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:05.166
<b>an individual who guides others </b>

134
00:08:05.166 --> 00:08:06.916
<b>is a leader.</b>

135
00:08:06.916 --> 00:08:09.708
<b>A leader is followed by others,</b>

136
00:08:09.708 --> 00:08:15.125
<b>and to make decisions that impact all those who</b>
<b>are influenced by them, is their responsibility.</b>

137
00:08:15.125 --> 00:08:16.416
<b>Making the right decisions,</b>

138
00:08:16.416 --> 00:08:21.375
<b>especially those that affect others, </b>

139
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:24.333
<b>is not an easy responsibility; </b>

140
00:08:24.333 --> 00:08:27.708
<b>it is quite challenging.</b>

141
00:08:27.708 --> 00:08:32.708
<b>If all decisions were made solely based on logic,</b>

142
00:08:32.708 --> 00:08:37.750
<b>they would hurt the sentiments of others.</b>

143
00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:42.166
<b>After all, the people who follow</b>
<b>are human beings, aren't they?</b>

144
00:08:42.166 --> 00:08:45.458
<b>They are sensitive,</b>

145
00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:48.750
<b>and a leader must keep this in mind.</b>

146
00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.166
<b>On the other hand,</b>

147
00:08:50.166 --> 00:08:56.541
<b>if decisions were entirely driven</b>
<b>by emotions and feelings, </b>

148
00:08:56.541 --> 00:09:00.833
<b>everyone's sensitivities would pull</b>
<b>in different directions,</b>

149
00:09:00.833 --> 00:09:07.166
<b>and the chariot of decision-making would</b>
<b>become directionless and collapse right there.</b>

150
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:08.916
<b>So,</b>

151
00:09:08.916 --> 00:09:13.375
<b>how should these decisions be made?</b>

152
00:09:13.375 --> 00:09:18.000
<b>Through a balance of emotions and intelligence.</b>

153
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.333
<b>And it is to attain this balance</b>

154
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:24.708
<b>that the teachings of the</b>
<b>Bhagavad Gita are here for you.</b>

